  "id": "DrugBank_DB12141 - MONDO_18434",
  "verbalization": "Gilteritinib is associated with Acute Myeloid Leukemia With T(9;11)(p22;q23) through a pathway involving Idarubicin, as evidenced by multiple indirect indications. The drug is linked to two distinct subtypes of Acute Myeloid Leukemia—Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia With Maturation and Acute Myeloblastic Leukemia Without Maturation—both of which are associated with Idarubicin. This suggests that Gilteritinib may exert its therapeutic effect on a broader spectrum of AML subtypes, potentially through shared mechanisms of action or biological pathways. The presence of Idarubicin as a common downstream target indicates a possible role in the treatment of AML, though the exact mechanism of interaction between Gilteritinib and Idarubicin remains unclear. The evidence supports a potential repurposing of Gilteritinib for AML, particularly in cases where Idarubicin is used as a treatment, but further studies are needed to clarify the specific relationship and therapeutic implications.",
